
 Context

 Step 5 wired the /profile page to live DB data — the four
 dynamic sections (Activity tiles, Spending by category,
 Distribution, Recent expenses) all read all-time data via the
 three query helpers in database/queries.py. There is no way
 for the user to scope that data to a date window ("this
 month", "since Monday", "in July").

 Step 6 adds a from/to date filter on the profile page. The
 user picks a range via two <input type="date"> fields; the
 page re-renders with every section scoped to that range. Both
 bounds inclusive. Either bound optional — empty means "no
 bound on that side". Malformed values are silently dropped.
 Backwards is swapped, not rejected.

 This is purely a runtime WHERE change — no new tables,
 columns, or migrations. expenses.date is already TEXT in
 YYYY-MM-DD form, so lexicographic >= / <= is correct.

 The implementation lives in three files (app.py,
 database/queries.py, templates/profile.html) and adds new
 tests in tests/. The existing Step 5 tests must still pass
 unchanged because the new parameters are optional with None
 defaults.

