 Risks & non-goals

 - Risk: adding kwargs to helper signatures could break tests
 that call them positionally. Mitigation: mark new params as
 keyword-only with *; existing call sites still work.
 - Risk: date_from / date_to accidentally interpolated into
 SQL string. Mitigation: every value goes through ?
 placeholders via a list of params; only the static AND glue
 comes from f"…".
 - Risk: an empty filtered range producing total = 0.0 in
 get_category_breakdown triggers a divide-by-zero. Mitigation:
 the existing if total == 0.0 branch already handles that.
 - Non-goal: no /expenses listing page yet (later step); the
 filter is profile-only.
 - Non-goal: no JS-driven date pickers, no presets ("this
 month"), no persisted filter across sessions — the URL is the
 source of truth.